Task 1: Configure Red Hat Satellite to Use IdM for Authentication
Subtask 1.1: Verify IdM Server Status
First, let's ensure our IdM server is running properly and accessible.

Connect to the IdM server:
ssh root@idm.example.com
Check IdM server status:
ipactl status
Verify IdM services are running:
systemctl status ipa
Test IdM web interface accessibility:
curl -k https://idm.example.com/ipa/ui/
Subtask 1.2: Prepare IdM for Satellite Integration
Create a service account for Satellite in IdM:
kinit admin
ipa user-add satellite-service --first=Satellite --last=Service --password
Create a dedicated group for Satellite administrators:
ipa group-add satellite-admins --desc="Satellite Administrators"
Add the service account to the group:
ipa group-add-member satellite-admins --users=satellite-service
Create additional test users:
ipa user-add testuser1 --first=Test --last=User1 --password
ipa user-add testuser2 --first=Test --last=User2 --password
Subtask 1.3: Configure Satellite Server for IdM Authentication
Connect to the Satellite server:
ssh root@satellite.example.com
Install required packages for LDAP integration:
dnf install -y foreman-installer python3-ldap
Configure Satellite to use IdM LDAP:
satellite-installer \
  --foreman-ipa-authentication=true \
  --foreman-ipa-server=idm.example.com \
  --foreman-ipa-realm=EXAMPLE.COM
Verify Satellite configuration:
satellite-maintain service status
Subtask 1.4: Configure LDAP Authentication Settings
Access Satellite web interface:

Open browser to https://satellite.example.com
Login with admin credentials
Navigate to LDAP configuration:

Go to Administer → Authentication Sources
Click Create Auth Source
Configure LDAP settings:

# Use these settings in the web interface:
# Name: IdM-LDAP
# Host: idm.example.com
# Port: 636
# LDAPS: Yes
# Account: uid=satellite-service,cn=users,cn=accounts,dc=example,dc=com
# Base DN: cn=users,cn=accounts,dc=example,dc=com
# Groups base DN: cn=groups,cn=accounts,dc=example,dc=com
# LDAP filter: (objectClass=person)
# Automatically create accounts: Yes
Test LDAP connection:
# From Satellite server command line
ldapsearch -x -H ldaps://idm.example.com:636 \
  -D "uid=satellite-service,cn=users,cn=accounts,dc=example,dc=com" \
  -W -b "cn=users,cn=accounts,dc=example,dc=com" \
  "(objectClass=person)"
Task 2: Enroll RHEL Systems into Satellite Using IdM Credentials
Subtask 2.1: Prepare Client Systems
Connect to client1:
ssh root@client1.example.com
Install IdM client packages:
dnf install -y ipa-client
Join client1 to IdM domain:
ipa-client-install \
  --server=idm.example.com \
  --domain=example.com \
  --realm=EXAMPLE.COM \
  --principal=admin \
  --password=your_admin_password \
  --unattended
Verify IdM client enrollment:
ipa-client-install --uninstall --unattended
kinit admin
klist
Subtask 2.2: Install Satellite Client Tools
Download Satellite client repository:
curl -o katello-ca-consumer-latest.noarch.rpm \
  https://satellite.example.com/pub/katello-ca-consumer-latest.noarch.rpm
Install the repository package:
rpm -Uvh katello-ca-consumer-latest.noarch.rpm
Install Satellite client tools:
dnf install -y katello-agent subscription-manager
Subtask 2.3: Register Systems with Satellite
Create activation key in Satellite (via web interface):

Navigate to Content → Activation Keys
Click Create Activation Key
Name: rhel8-key
Environment: Library
Content View: Default Organization View
Register client1 with Satellite:

subscription-manager register \
  --org="Default_Organization" \
  --activationkey="rhel8-key" \
  --serverurl=https://satellite.example.com:443/rhsm \
  --baseurl=https://satellite.example.com/pulp/repos
Verify registration:
subscription-manager status
subscription-manager list --installed
Repeat the process for client2:
ssh root@client2.example.com
# Repeat steps 2.1 through 2.3 for client2
Subtask 2.4: Configure Remote Execution
On Satellite server, enable remote execution:
satellite-installer --enable-foreman-plugin-remote-execution
Configure SSH keys for remote execution:
# Generate SSH key for foreman user
sudo -u foreman ssh-keygen -t rsa -b 4096 -N '' \
  -f /usr/share/foreman/.ssh/id_rsa
Distribute SSH keys to clients:
# Copy public key to clients
ssh-copy-id -i /usr/share/foreman/.ssh/id_rsa.pub root@client1.example.com
ssh-copy-id -i /usr/share/foreman/.ssh/id_rsa.pub root@client2.example.com
